 to be provided  for us and so I mean you know if you get  a starbucks coffee twice a day and that  cost you six dollars you don't think  that's a problem but you know you don't  want to spend you know 120 hundred and  thirty dollars to go to the doctor I'm  to find out you know why you have you  know sore throat or you know a pain in  your stomach or whatever so people have  become very you know sort of overtaken  by the fact that people now think health  care is an entitlement that the  government should provide and you know  we're spending 17.3 percent of our gross  domestic product on health care and  people said well it's way too much  Canada spends 10 we yes Canada spends 10  because the government says that's what  we can afford and then you get those  long waiting lists denied care and lack  of access to the latest technology you  know I'm part of the baby boom  generation you know we're all going to  when we retire there's gonna be a whole  flood of new people you know that are  going to have to go on Medicare and we  know it's you know it's being cut by  five hundred twenty nine billion over  ten years we're going to have a hard  time finding doctors  and having access to the best care but  you know we need to voucherize Medicare  we need to voucherize Medicaid there's a  whole bunch of things that can be done  to empower doctors and patients and keep  our health care system alive but it's  not going to happen it's going to be  destroyed under this takeover of our  system since Obamacare has already  passed is it too late for us what can we  do now I favor repeal and replace now if  the Republicans take over the house this  fall and if they even take the Senate  that is not going to be enough for  repeal and replace that the Republicans  would have to take the presidential  office in 2012 and Congress and then  early in 2013 they would have to work  very hard on repeal and replace but it  also means having a strong leader who  can sort of heard all these cats so that  they focus on repeal and replace and  then we can build with a health care  system which I talked about in my book  empowering doctors and patients changing  the tax code reducing getting States to  reduce their mandates allowing people to  buy insurance across state lines all of  these things but if they don't you know  as Milton Friedman used to always say to  me Sally tell me a government program  that has ever been eliminated you know  the angora mohair subsidy program very  few are ever you know eliminated so  we've got to get on this right away and  but it will take a lot of willpower and  a strong leader to make it happen
 

